# Testing and validation

## Non-negotiables

- Never weaken, skip, delete, disable, or narrow a test to make an
  implementation pass. If a test blocks a change, report the conflict and stop.
- Never fabricate, predict, or summarise test results from expectation. Paste
  executed output.
- Never claim a test suite passed without running it.
- A Cursor checkpoint is not evidence. Real Git history and real command output
  are.

## Commands this repository actually provides

```
./tools/unix/build_omim.sh -d                                   # desktop debug with tests
./tools/unix/build_omim.sh -d <target>                          # single target
./tools/unix/run_tests.sh -b ../omim-build-debug -s smoke       # smoke suite (baseline reference; not a V1 gate — see README §8.2)
./tools/unix/run_tests.sh -b ../omim-build-debug -f "<regex>"    # filter by name
cd ../omim-build-debug && ctest -L "omim-test" --output-on-failure
cd android && ./gradlew -Pandroidauto=true lint                  # Android lint
./tools/unix/clang-format.sh                                    # formatting check
```

## Known CI gap

`.forgejo/workflows/linux-check.yaml` runs the tests but its
`CTEST_EXCLUDE_REGEX` currently excludes `map_tests`, `routing_tests`,
`indexer_tests`, and most other suites. `.github/workflows/` has no C++ test job
at all. A test added to an excluded target will not run in CI. Check where a new
test will actually execute before claiming it is covered.

## Adding tests

- New test targets use `omim_add_test` from `cmake/OmimTesting.cmake` and are
  registered with `omim_add_test_subdirectory`. Prefer the lightest option set;
  `REQUIRE_QT` and `REQUIRE_SERVER` make a target slow and are only for tests
  that genuinely need a Qt event loop or a test server.
- Street Pixels logic tests belong in `street_pixels_tests`, not in `map_tests`.
- The desktop smoke suite is baseline reference only (README §8.2); it is not a
  Street Pixels V1 merge gate. SP-002 adds `street_pixels_tests` as the C++ CI gate.
- Test thresholds at their boundaries, on both sides. A GPS acceptance rule with
  a 25-metre limit needs a case just inside and just outside.
- Prefer synthetic `location::GpsInfo` sequences over device-dependent tests for
  anything that can be expressed deterministically.
- Android has three JVM unit-test files and no instrumented test infrastructure.
  Do not assume instrumentation exists.

## Manual validation

Some Street Pixels behaviour cannot be verified without hardware: background and
screen-off recording, GPS quality in real environments, battery, and rendering
performance. For those, record device model, OS version, build type, route or
procedure, and the observed result. "Tested, works" is not a record.

Follow the ten-step validation workflow in `docs/implementation/README.md` §8.
Do not declare a work item accepted; report evidence and let a human decide.
